\section PETSUV_Introduction Introduction

The PET SUV Calculation view converts a PET image into a Standardized
Uptake Value (SUV) image. The generated SUV map is added as a child
node of the selected PET image and can be visualized or analysed like
any other image. SUV computation follows the IBSI-SUV benchmark
recommendations.

The view requires DICOM-tagged PET input. Acquisition information
(patient weight / height / sex, injected activity, half-life, decay
correction strategy, units) is read from the input's DICOM properties
and may be overridden via the controls below.

\image html usage_suv.png "The PET SUV Calculation view."

\section PETSUV_Usage Usage

-# Select a PET image in the \b PET \b node \b selector at the top of
   the view. With \b Select \b only \b PET \b images enabled (default),
   only nodes whose DICOM Modality tag (0008,0060) is \c PT can be
   selected.
-# Choose the desired SUV variant from the \b SUV \b variant combo.
   The \b Patient group always shows body weight; the height and sex
   fields appear only for variants that consume them (LBM, IBW, BSA).
   All fields are auto-populated from DICOM and can be overridden
   manually.
-# For activity-concentration input, review and, if needed, override
   the fields in the \b Radiopharmaceutical \b / \b activity group
   (\b Injected \b activity, \b Radio \b nuclide / \b half-life).
   Picking a nuclide from the combo sets the half-life; manually
   editing the half-life flips the combo to <em>(custom)</em>. This
   group, and the \b Time \b to \b measurement section below, are
   hidden when the input is already a pre-normalized SUV, since
   neither applies.
-# Inspect the \b Time \b to \b measurement section: in \b Auto
   \b detect mode (default), the decay-correction strategy is derived
   from DICOM and shown as the \b Strategy label, and the
   per-(timestep, slice) decay durations populate the read-only
   tree-view below. The other two modes are described in
   \ref PETSUV_DecayTime.
-# When the diagnostics widget reports \b Configuration \b OK, click
   \b Calculate \b SUV. A new node named
   <tt>&lt;selected-node-name&gt;_SUV</tt>
   is added as a child of the selected PET node. The SUV image has
   <tt>double</tt> pixel type regardless of the input pixel type.

\section PETSUV_Variants Variants and patient measurements

The variant combo lists the five supported SUV normalizations:
- \b BW (body weight)
- \b LBM-Janmahasatian (lean body mass, Janmahasatian 2005)
- \b LBM-James128 (lean body mass, James 1976 with factor 1.28)
- \b IBW (ideal body weight, Sugawara 1999)
- \b BSA (body surface area, DuBois 1916)

Each variant declares the patient measurements it consumes. The body
weight field is always shown; the height and sex fields appear only
when the selected variant needs them:
- \b BW needs only body weight.
- \b LBM-Janmahasatian / \b LBM-James128 need weight, height, and sex.
- \b IBW needs height and sex (weight is shown but not used by the formula).
- \b BSA needs weight and height.

For sex-specific variants, an ambiguous patient sex
(\c O <em>Other</em>, or absent / unresolved) triggers the IBSI-SUV
mean-of-male-and-female adaptation under
\b DICOMReadPolicy::Lenient (logged as a warning). Under
\b DICOMReadPolicy::Strict (see \ref PETSUV_Validation), the
adaptation is refused and the user is prompted to supply an
unambiguous sex override.

\section PETSUV_DecayTime Decay-time mode

The \b Time \b to \b measurement group offers three modes:

- \b Auto \b detect (default). Decay durations are derived per
  (timestep, slice) following the IBSI-SUV strategy chain
  (DICOM Decay Correction = ADMIN / START / NONE, vendor private
  datetime tags, AcquisitionTime / SeriesTime fallbacks). The
  detected strategy is shown as the \b Strategy label; the
  per-(timestep, slice) values populate the read-only tree-view
  below.

- \b User \b defined \b (uniform). A single decay duration is applied
  uniformly to every voxel. Enter the value (in minutes) in the
  spinbox next to the radio button. The DICOM decay-correction
  pipeline is bypassed entirely; the strategy reads \em "User-defined
  decay time".

- \b User \b defined \b (per-slice, edit in table below). The
  per-(timestep, slice) decay-time map becomes editable in the
  tree-view. The map is seeded from the currently effective values
  when this mode is engaged, so the user starts editing from the
  Auto-detected baseline rather than from zero. Every cell edit is
  pushed to the filter immediately; the diagnostics widget surfaces
  any validation failure (for example, an out-of-range slice index
  or a map shape that no longer matches the image geometry).

The uniform and per-slice overrides are mutually exclusive by design;
toggling between modes clears the previously engaged slot.

A decay-timing problem (ambiguous auto-detection, or an invalid or
conflicting manual override) is shown on the \b Strategy line in the
warning colour, not only in the diagnostics widget.

\section PETSUV_Validation Validation controls

The \b Validation group holds three persistent toggles that affect
how borderline DICOM input is handled. Toggle changes immediately
re-run the configuration; the diagnostics widget reflects the new
state.

- \b Force \b PET \b semantics. Bypass the (0008,0060) Modality == "PT"
  check. Use only on data that is genuinely PET but ships an incorrect
  Modality tag.

- \b Force \b activity-concentration \b semantics \b ([Bq/mL]).
  Treat the input pixel values as activity concentration regardless
  of (0054,1001) Units. Required for inputs whose Units value is
  outside the documented set the pipeline supports
  (BQML / GML / CM2ML / CNTS with Philips private factor) but that
  are nonetheless in [Bq/mL]. Only physically meaningful if the
  pixels really are [Bq/mL].

- \b Strict \b DICOM \b input \b policy. Refuse the IBSI-SUV
  recommended empirical adaptations of borderline DICOM input
  (sub-1e4 Radionuclide Total Dose reinterpreted as MBq, vendor-
  specific decay-timing fallbacks, ambiguous patient sex). Each
  refused adaptation surfaces a typed exception with a per-category
  actionable message in the diagnostics widget.

\section PETSUV_Diagnostics Diagnostics widget

The diagnostics widget below the validation group renders two
blocks:

-# An <em>Auto-detected</em> summary of what the filter deduced from
   the input: vendor, pixel semantics, injected dose, half-life,
   decay-correction strategy, tracer index, and the active policy
   / overrides.
-# An actionable message: either \b Configuration \b OK or a
   per-category hint mapped from the typed exception raised by the
   filter (missing DICOM property, invalid DICOM property,
   ambiguous decay timing, missing variant input, unsupported
   units, missing Philips scale, vendor-empirical decay refused,
   implausible dose, ambiguous-sex adaptation refused, generic
   benchmark adaptation required).

The \b Calculate \b SUV button is enabled exactly when the
configuration is OK.

